<spell-notebook "include theming">
	<header level="1">
		Include
		<header>An include shows part of another page from this site in this one, loaded at once, when idle or when
              scrolled into view.</>
	</>
	<include-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  no tokens of its own;  what reaches the included markup instead. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			An include has no look of its own, so no `--ui-include-*` tokens. What styles the included markup:

			- In a shadow root (the default): only inherited values reach it -- fonts, colours and every `--ui-*` token set
			  on the include or above it. Style the box with `::part(content)`.
			- With `page-styles`: the page's own stylesheets, as for any other light-DOM markup.
			- The loader and the error message are `::part(loader)` and `::part(error)`.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			ui-include.notes {
			  --ui-font-size: 14px;
			  color: var(--ui-grey);
			}
			ui-include.notes::part(content) {
			  padding: 1em;
			}
			```
		</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-include" playground>
				<ui-include source="/components/ui/examples/release-notes.html">Loading the release notes...</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			Include is ours, not Fomantic's, and draws nothing itself, so no theme restyles it. The `ui-*` elements in the
			included markup follow the site's theme like any others.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
